WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.221
When Ben reached his block, he heard leaves rustling behind him.

2
00:00:09.222 --> 00:00:14.116
He turned and saw the black kitten looking up at him.

3
00:00:14.117 --> 00:00:18.275
She wiggled her back end and leaped toward Ben's feet.

4
00:00:18.276 --> 00:00:20.801
Ben's first thought was to flee.

5
00:00:20.802 --> 00:00:24.009
Then he realized the kitten wasn't hissing.

6
00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:27.649
She was playing.

7
00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:30.647
"Weird," Ben thought.

8
00:00:30.648 --> 00:00:36.932
"The other night this kitten was attacking me. But now she likes me."

9
00:00:36.933 --> 00:00:39.690
Suddenly Ben realized something.

10
00:00:39.691 --> 00:00:45.312
"It's because I smell like fish! Of course! Cats love fish."

11
00:00:45.313 --> 00:00:49.166
Ben laughed. "Well, sorry, kitten.

12
00:00:49.167 --> 00:00:52.383
I'm not going to smell like this for long. See you later."

13
00:00:52.384 --> 00:00:54.654
He floated away.

14
00:00:54.655 --> 00:00:59.400
The kitten followed him all the way home.

15
00:00:59.401 --> 00:01:03.058
When Ben opened the door, the kitten darted inside.

16
00:01:03.059 --> 00:01:10.725
"Hey!" Ben cried. The kitten ran down the hallway.

17
00:01:10.726 --> 00:01:13.827
"Ahh!" Ben's little brother screamed.

18
00:01:13.828 --> 00:01:17.669
"What's going on?" Ben's mom called from another room.

19
00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:20.977
"Um, nothing, Mom!" Ben went to his room.

20
00:01:20.978 --> 00:01:25.556
The kitten had Sid backed into a corner.

21
00:01:25.557 --> 00:01:34.348
"G-get this kitten away from me!" Sid cried.

22
00:01:34.349 --> 00:01:38.060
The kitten pranced over to Ben and purred.

23
00:01:38.061 --> 00:01:39.745
Sid calmed down.

24
00:01:39.746 --> 00:01:44.608
"Why isn't it attacking—" Sid covered his nose.

25
00:01:44.609 --> 00:01:48.797
"Ugh! You smell like dead fish!"

26
00:01:48.798 --> 00:01:55.406
"That's why the kitten's not attacking me."

27
00:01:55.407 --> 00:02:00.440
The kitten curled up on Ben's bed and went to sleep.

28
00:02:00.441 --> 00:02:03.913
Ben couldn't help smiling.

29
00:02:03.914 --> 00:02:15.567
That night the kitten ran around wildly.

30
00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:24.336
When the sun rose Thursday morning, the kitten was sleeping peacefully.

31
00:02:24.337 --> 00:02:28.039
Ben and Sid were exhausted.

32
00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:36.530
Ben yawned as he pulled on his hoodie.

33
00:02:36.531 --> 00:02:40.263
"We'll figure out what to do with the kitten later," he told Sid.

34
00:02:40.264 --> 00:02:45.887
"Meanwhile don't say anything to Mom or Dad. I have to get to school."

35
00:02:45.888 --> 00:02:53.151
Since talking to Winnie, Ben had decided to work hard in Cooking class.

36
00:02:53.152 --> 00:02:59.807
He was busy grinding grubs when monsters started noticing a strange smell.

37
00:02:59.808 --> 00:03:03.336
"I smell hot sauce," a mummy said.

38
00:03:03.337 --> 00:03:06.738
Ben sniffed.

39
00:03:06.739 --> 00:03:12.598
He and Waldo must have missed some of the sauce when they were cleaning it up the day before.

40
00:03:12.599 --> 00:03:15.677
"I smell it too," Mr. Icky said.

41
00:03:15.678 --> 00:03:19.587
"But nobody should be using that in today's recipe."

42
00:03:19.588 --> 00:03:23.539
He walked around the room.

43
00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:26.157
"Where is it coming from?"

44
00:03:26.158 --> 00:03:30.245
Ben almost told Mr. Icky about yesterday's hot sauce spill.

45
00:03:30.246 --> 00:03:35.122
He stopped himself. "I can't tell Mr. Icky," he thought.

46
00:03:35.123 --> 00:03:40.662
"Waldo and I will be in big trouble for using the cooking equipment without permission."

47
00:03:40.663 --> 00:03:48.858
"Mr. Icky!" Mog said. "That wall is vibrating."

48
00:03:48.859 --> 00:03:55.504
Mr. Icky stared at the wall in surprise. "Huh. You're right."

49
00:03:55.505 --> 00:04:00.075
"I hope the hot sauce isn't causing that," Ben thought.

50
00:04:00.076 --> 00:04:05.388
Mr. Icky slid over to the intercom and pressed a button.

51
00:04:05.389 --> 00:04:08.784
"Principal's office," the office ogre said.

52
00:04:08.785 --> 00:04:14.317
"Please send Mr. Freaky down to the cooking classroom," Mr. Icky said.

53
00:04:14.318 --> 00:04:20.571
A moment later Mr. Freaky hurried into the room, his noses wiggling.

54
00:04:20.572 --> 00:04:23.915
"Don't tell me we have a problem!"

55
00:04:23.916 --> 00:04:26.612
Mr. Icky held up his tentacles.

56
00:04:26.613 --> 00:04:29.417
"I figured I should let you know about that."

57
00:04:29.418 --> 00:04:33.193
He pointed at the vibrating wall.

58
00:04:33.194 --> 00:04:39.479
Mr. Freaky went over for a closer look.

59
00:04:39.480 --> 00:04:41.259
"What's causing it?"

60
00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:44.237
"We don't know," Mr. Icky said.

61
00:04:44.238 --> 00:04:48.059
"There's also a smell. It smells like—"

62
00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:51.277
"Hot sauce," Mr. Freaky said.

63
00:04:51.278 --> 00:04:58.687
He took out a handkerchief and blew his noses.

64
00:04:58.688 --> 00:05:00.930
"I'll have Mr. Bog look into it.

65
00:05:00.931 --> 00:05:05.049
We can't have any problems during the cooking competition tomorrow.

66
00:05:05.050 --> 00:05:08.806
Everything must go perfectly!"

67
00:05:08.807 --> 00:05:12.373
The principal hurried out.

68
00:05:12.374 --> 00:05:16.992
A minute later Mr. Bog came in.

69
00:05:16.993 --> 00:05:23.587
The custodian sniffed and poked the wall.

70
00:05:23.588 --> 00:05:29.218
Then he got down on his hands and knees and looked behind the cabinet.

71
00:05:29.219 --> 00:05:32.489
"I smell hot sauce," he said.

72
00:05:32.490 --> 00:05:38.269
"Maybe I should say something," Ben thought.

73
00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:44.880
Mr. Bog backed out from behind the cabinet.

74
00:05:44.881 --> 00:05:49.350
"I don't know why the wall is vibrating. But I found this stuff."

75
00:05:49.351 --> 00:05:57.928
The custodian placed several items on the counter: a few bat claws, coins, three socks, and a necklace.

76
00:05:57.929 --> 00:06:00.098
"That's it!" Ben thought.

77
00:06:00.099 --> 00:06:02.944
He forgot all about the hot sauce.

78
00:06:02.945 --> 00:06:08.246
"I'll get Winnie a necklace for her birthday!"

79
00:06:08.247 --> 00:06:13.692
After school Ben hurried into Ghoulie's Jewelry Shop.

80
00:06:13.693 --> 00:06:17.949
"Good afternoon, young man," Mrs. Ghoulie said.

81
00:06:17.950 --> 00:06:20.559
"What can I do for you?"

82
00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:23.741
"I want to buy a necklace," Ben said.

83
00:06:23.742 --> 00:06:32.295
"For a special someone?" Mrs. Ghoulie chuckled.

84
00:06:32.296 --> 00:06:35.783
She pulled a sparkly necklace out of the jewelry case.

85
00:06:35.784 --> 00:06:38.031
"This is one of my favorites.

86
00:06:38.032 --> 00:06:40.281
It's three thousand dollars.

87
00:06:40.282 --> 00:06:45.193
But I can give it to you for $2,500."

88
00:06:45.194 --> 00:06:50.500
Ben gulped. "I can't afford that!"

89
00:06:50.501 --> 00:06:53.961
"What's your budget?" Mrs. Ghoulie asked.

90
00:06:53.962 --> 00:06:57.479
Ben took out his wallet and looked inside.

91
00:06:57.480 --> 00:07:02.700
He grinned sheepishly. "I have sixteen dollars."

92
00:07:02.701 --> 00:07:07.351
Mrs. Ghoulie pointed at a small rack at the end of the counter.

93
00:07:07.352 --> 00:07:10.580
"Perhaps you'll find something there."

94
00:07:10.581 --> 00:07:13.074
Ben went over to the rack.

95
00:07:13.075 --> 00:07:16.911
He saw a necklace for fifteen dollars.

96
00:07:16.912 --> 00:07:23.116
It wasn't sparkly, but it had smooth green stones the same color as Winnie's eyes.

97
00:07:23.117 --> 00:07:26.684
"It's the thought that counts," Ben told himself.

98
00:07:26.685 --> 00:07:36.187
He looked back at Mrs. Ghoulie. "I'll take this one."

